From: lenOS <security@lenos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] lenOS: security panel at the top of Settings

Adds a lenOS category above every other homepage category, opening a
fragment with: DNS enforcement and time-sync shield toggles, the strict
firewall with VPN UID allowlist, an LTE-only radio switch (drops the
2G/3G downgrade surface via TelephonyManager; GrapheneOS LTE-only is
partial here — 5G stays), a captive-portal detection switch (default
off: Settings.Global captive_portal_mode=0 IGNORE, the only documented
probe-free value; on writes 1 PROMPT, the stock behavior), and system
app removal for user 0.

State lives in Settings.Global; the lenos-netd daemon in system_ext
applies it kernel-side. The Settings app already declares
WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS, DELETE_PACKAGES and MODIFY_PHONE_STATE and runs
as the system UID, so no manifest or privapp whitelist changes are
required. No lenOS strings enter build props; the panel strings live
inside the Settings app only.

